00:10:01.839 --> 00:10:05.519
vendors. One of the easiest ways to make

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:07.200
more money right now. And the other area

00:10:05.519 --> 00:10:08.720
you want to optimize for is your time.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:10.560
So in a scale business, you're going to

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:11.777
be working constantly. I'm sorry, it

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:13.519
sucks. You just need to know this.

00:10:11.777 --> 00:10:15.519
[music] We're not going to be at a party

00:10:13.519 --> 00:10:17.760
for a weekend. In a lifestyle business,

00:10:15.519 --> 00:10:19.920
on the other hand, you got you got it.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:22.079
You go take the jet somewhere else. Now,

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:24.320
here's how I would set this up if I was

00:10:22.079 --> 00:10:25.600
you. First, your team. You don't want to

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:27.760
build a huge team. Like, if you're

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:29.600
trying to scale, you actually want a

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:32.000
lean, scrappy team that can wear a few

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:33.392
hats. The most important hire here is

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:34.560
probably a really good number two.

00:10:33.392 --> 00:10:35.760
[music] like they're going to handle a

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:36.880
lot of the day-to-day things. If

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:39.440
something breaks in the middle of the

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:42.160
night, it goes to you, not them. A good

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:44.959
one's going to cost you probably not

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:46.640
less than 100k, maybe 150k with some

00:10:44.959 --> 00:10:48.399
aligned incentives on the performance of

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:50.160
the company. So again, you're trying to

00:10:48.399 --> 00:10:52.320
make more profit. So you give them

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:54.399
bonuses if they find ways to decrease

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:56.160
your costs or increase your topline

00:10:54.399 --> 00:10:56.880
revenue, keeping the margin the same.

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:59.040
Second [music]

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:01.440
is only doing the things that you need

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:03.600
to do. So, it's like, [music]

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:05.279
is it you or can it be someone else?

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:06.720
This applies to every type of business,

00:11:05.279 --> 00:11:07.920
but is especially important if you're

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:09.839
trying to maximize time in your

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:13.519
lifestyle [music] business. I use a

00:11:09.839 --> 00:11:15.360
delegation killbox. It's on page 254 of

00:11:13.519 --> 00:11:17.680
the book. It's basically three

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:19.680
questions. The first question is, could

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:21.680
somebody [music] else do this? If no,

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:24.800
keep it for now. Second question is,

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:26.720
have I taught someone how to do this? If

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:30.079
no, teach someone right now. Three is

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:31.279
have I let them do it without me? If no,

00:11:30.079 --> 00:11:33.760
pick a day [music] to hand over the task

00:11:31.279 --> 00:11:36.240
within 14 days. But here's the thing,

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:38.000
profit and time are not completely

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:39.839
separate from each other. If you stop

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:41.360
working on your business completely,

00:11:39.839 --> 00:11:43.360
your time is going to go up, but your

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:44.560
profit will most likely go down. So, I

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:46.880
usually measure the health of a

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:48.959
lifestyle business by profit per hour of

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:50.480
your time. Some of the deals are going

00:11:48.959 --> 00:11:52.160
to cost you a lot more time, won't

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:53.760
really move the needle in your business.

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:56.240
This is the only path where you can say,

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:58.240
"H, I'm full-on with clients. I'm I'm

00:11:56.240 --> 00:11:59.680
great. No thanks. I'm good."

00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:01.440
The last path you [music] can take in

00:11:59.680 --> 00:12:03.360
business is the exit path, which means

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:05.120
you are optimizing to sell. This is

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:06.420
where you obsess over the price tag.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:08.160
Everything you do when planning for

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:10.000
[music] an exit is designed to increase

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:12.560
your price so you leave with the biggest

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:14.320
payout possible. So your income in this

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:18.399
type of business, it's going to look

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:19.760
more like this and then nothing cuz

00:12:18.399 --> 00:12:23.200
you're going to sell. So, you're going

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:24.560
to make a little less than a lifestyle

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:26.959
business here because you're wanting to

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:28.800
keep all the profit in the business, but

00:12:26.959 --> 00:12:30.560
you're going to have a huge check on

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:32.480
closing day and then you're going to be

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:35.440
out of the business. Probably no

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:37.040
recurring revenue or consistent stream.

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:38.320
So, if you absolutely love the business

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:39.920
and want to keep working on it for a

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:41.839
while, this isn't for you. This is for

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:43.600
people who want to get in, grow, get

00:12:41.839 --> 00:12:45.440
out, and make a lot of money. And maybe

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:47.519
you want to go on to your next product

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:49.040
or your next business. Like we have

00:12:47.519 --> 00:12:50.880
multiple members of our contrarian

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:53.279
boardroom who are like, "Okay, I like to

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:54.560
scale businesses to a million bucks. The

00:12:53.279 --> 00:12:55.600
second it gets at a million bucks, I

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:57.200
like to sell it because I don't really

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:58.720
know how to get to 10." So, how do you

00:12:57.200 --> 00:13:00.160
do this? There are two numbers that

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:02.399
determine how much your company will

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:04.880
sell for. [music] SDE, sellers

00:13:02.399 --> 00:13:06.560
discretionary earnings. That's basically

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:08.560
like saying how much money you put in

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:11.440
your pocket as the [music] owner and the

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:12.880
multiple. So, SDE means how much money

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:15.200
are you actually making from the

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:17.040
business. This means you take the net

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:19.440
income of the business. You're going to

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:22.160
add your salary. You're going to add any

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:23.839
benefits the company provided like that

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:26.480
trip to Greece that you expensed because

00:13:23.839 --> 00:13:29.519
you actually did work on it. And then

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:32.160
any large one-time expenses that will

00:13:29.519 --> 00:13:33.680
not have to be repeated. To grow SD, you

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:36.320
want to grow the profit of the company

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:38.959
as quickly as humanly possible. So that

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:40.800
is the difference between a scale and a

00:13:38.959 --> 00:13:43.120
lifestyle business. You're looking for

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:45.279
more profits in a lifestyle business.

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:48.800
scale. You're actually optimizing not

00:13:45.279 --> 00:13:50.959
for cash but for usually market share of

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:53.169
the business. Both can become an exit

00:13:50.959 --> 00:13:55.360
business but not with the same strategy.

00:13:53.169 --> 00:13:58.480
[music] Now the multiple is where you

00:13:55.360 --> 00:14:03.440
make a lot more money on the exit. So if

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:05.199
SDE is you know 200K at a 3x multiple

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:08.959
that means you can sell the business for

00:14:05.199 --> 00:14:11.279
600K right? If it's a 5x multiple

00:14:08.959 --> 00:14:13.360
instead of a three, well, that means now

00:14:11.279 --> 00:14:15.440
you sell the business for a million

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:17.600
bucks. Think of the multiple as an

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:19.920
indication of the risk, like the

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:22.000
durability, the growth, how easy it is

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:24.480
to transfer the business. A business

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:26.240
that runs on one person doing everything

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:29.199
from their kitchen counter, well, you're

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:30.480
going to sell for probably 1x or lower.

00:14:29.199 --> 00:14:32.240
If you have a business where you have an

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:35.279
executive team instead of alignment

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:37.680
compensation that means that that owner

00:14:35.279 --> 00:14:39.839
manages the systems and makes strategic

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:42.240
decisions and thus the multiple is going

00:14:39.839 --> 00:14:44.800
to be a lot higher for the business.

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:46.320
Also industry really matters. So

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:48.639
software has one of the highest

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:51.120
multiples and one of the lower multiples

00:14:48.639 --> 00:14:53.519
is going to be service businesses. There

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:55.440
are basically four areas I want you to

00:14:53.519 --> 00:14:57.040
focus on to increase the multiple that

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:59.519
you can sell your business for and make

00:14:57.040 --> 00:15:01.519
a ton of money. The first one is called

00:14:59.519 --> 00:15:03.040
owner dependency, which if everything

00:15:01.519 --> 00:15:04.800
relies on you as the owner, you're not

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:06.399
actually selling a business. You have a

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:08.320
job. You're trying to sell it and nobody

00:15:06.399 --> 00:15:10.320
wants to buy it. I see this all the

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:12.720
time. The business would actually cease

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:14.399
to exist if they don't work all of the

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:16.160
time. We don't want that. This is the

00:15:14.399 --> 00:15:18.399
reason why I actually wrote my new book,

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:19.680
Owner Beyond. It's my exact system on

00:15:18.399 --> 00:15:21.680
how I build a business that doesn't

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:23.360
fully depend on me. All right, so we've

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:25.839
talked about owner dependency. Now,

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:27.760
we've got recurring revenue. Recurring

00:15:25.839 --> 00:15:29.760
revenue is always going to trade at a

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:31.600
higher multiple than one-off revenue.

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:33.760
So, the more people that you have paying

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:35.199
you continuously as clients, the more

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:37.360
you're going to get to sell your company

00:15:35.199 --> 00:15:40.880
for. What's a good rule of thumb [music]

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:44.240
is basically one-time revenue trades at

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:47.360
3x. This is a generalistic one. And

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:48.800
recurring [music] revenue trades at 5x.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:50.959
So, if you're trying to exit, it makes

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:52.560
sense to charge someone less to get them

00:15:50.959 --> 00:15:54.000
on a subscription than a one-time

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:55.199
purchase. Isn't [music] that wild? So

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:57.519
you can basically see the difference

00:15:55.199 --> 00:15:59.040
here between the two. Now scale, you

00:15:57.519 --> 00:16:01.360
just [music] want maximum recurring

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:02.639
revenue. With lifestyle, profit is

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:04.639
profit and it doesn't really matter if

00:16:02.639 --> 00:16:07.199
it's one-offs or recurring. Although

00:16:04.639 --> 00:16:09.199
recurring is more stable. With exit, you

00:16:07.199 --> 00:16:10.959
can have a smaller total revenue if it

00:16:09.199 --> 00:16:12.320
is recurring compared to one time

00:16:10.959 --> 00:16:13.839
because again, you could have a business

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:15.360
that's 2x smaller, but if it's got

00:16:13.839 --> 00:16:18.320
recurring revenue, you could sell it for

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:19.839
more. Third is customer concentration,

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:22.480
which means how much of your revenue

00:16:19.839 --> 00:16:25.759
comes from one customer or a small

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:28.959
subset. [music] If 10% of your customers

00:16:25.759 --> 00:16:30.320
generate more than 50% of your revenue,

00:16:28.959 --> 00:16:32.079
then you have something called customer

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:34.079
concentration. So the mark every

00:16:32.079 --> 00:16:36.399
business should be thinking about is how

00:16:34.079 --> 00:16:38.480
do we get our business to make sure that

00:16:36.399 --> 00:16:40.800
we have more customers and those

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:42.880
customers have less with us

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:45.199
individually. [music] It really depends

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:47.199
percentage-wise per industry. So some

00:16:45.199 --> 00:16:48.711
businesses it might be 20%, other

00:16:47.199 --> 00:16:49.279
businesses it might be 30 or 40%.

00:16:48.711 --> 00:16:51.360
[music]

00:16:49.279 --> 00:16:52.880
So if you're optimizing for an exit, you

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:54.560
have to diversify the number of

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:56.560
customers [music] you have. You actually

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:58.560
want a lot more as opposed to one big

00:16:56.560 --> 00:17:00.880
one. And then finally, we've got growth

00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:03.040
trajectory, which is a business with

00:17:00.880 --> 00:17:04.959
500K [music] in profit, growing at 10%

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:08.559
annually, is worth more than a business

00:17:04.959 --> 00:17:11.199
at 500K profit, but growing at 3%. And

00:17:08.559 --> 00:17:13.520
then growth trajectory. So a business

00:17:11.199 --> 00:17:14.799
that is growing at 10% annually is worth

00:17:13.520 --> 00:17:16.720
more than a business that's growing at

00:17:14.799 --> 00:17:17.919
3%. You don't need to be a genius to

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:19.280
figure that out. But if you're

00:17:17.919 --> 00:17:20.880
optimizing for the sale, [music] you

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:22.959
really have to manage the fact that you

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:24.959
want profits to grow up. But ideally,

00:17:22.959 --> 00:17:27.039
you'd also like growth, aka revenue

00:17:24.959 --> 00:17:29.322
growth, to go up. You can have a great

00:17:27.039 --> 00:17:31.679
business, amazing SDE, and optimize

